  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given planes are\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& P: x+y-2 z+7=0 \\\\\n& Q: x+y+2 z+2=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nand $R: 3 x+3 y-6 z-11=0$\nConsider Plane $P$ and $R$.\nHere $a_1=1, b_1=1, c_1=-2$ and $a_2=3, b_2=3, c_2=-6$\nSince, $\\frac{a_1}{a_2}=\\frac{b_1}{b_2}=\\frac{c_1}{c_2}=\\frac{1}{3}$ therefore $P$ and $R$ are parallel.",
    "image": null
  },
